From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haroldxie <xiewenhao2308@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: export aarch64_insn_patch_text_nosync() for the KJIT
 runtime's direct BL links

The KJIT runtime patches one instruction of a verified fragment in place:
a link slot, a `nop` that the runtime turns into `b <fragment>` while the
callee's fragment is live and back into `nop` when that fragment retires
(docs/pipeline.md, "Direct BL links (A16)"). The fragment images stay
read-only and executable; the write goes through the fixmap alias with
the data cache cleaned and the instruction cache invalidated, which is
exactly what aarch64_insn_patch_text_nosync() does for ftrace and jump
labels. `nop` and `b` are both in the architecture's list of instructions
that may be modified while another CPU executes them, so a CPU fetching the
slot concurrently runs either the old or the new word.

Export the function GPL-only. Nothing else changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c
@@ -193,6 +193,7 @@ int __kprobes aarch64_insn_patch_text_nosync(void *addr, u32 insn)
 
 	return ret;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(aarch64_insn_patch_text_nosync);
 
 struct aarch64_insn_patch {
 	void		**text_addrs;
-- 
